---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';

import shotMyReferrals from '../../../assets/guide/05-my-referrals.png';
---

<GuideLayout
  slug="track-your-referrals"
  title="Track a referral you have filed"
  description="Once a referral is with the counselling team, My Referrals is where you see what is happening without having to chase anyone."
  audience="For teachers"
  readingTime="2 min read"
>
  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Open My Referrals</h2>
      <p>
        From <strong>Classrooms</strong>, switch to the <strong>My Referrals</strong> tab. The
        number on the tab is how many of your referrals are still open.
      </p>
      <p>
        This list is yours alone. You will not see referrals filed by other teachers, even for
        students in your own class, and they will not see yours.
      </p>
      <figure>
        <Image
          src={shotMyReferrals}
          alt="The My Referrals tab showing two referrals: one in progress for Kabir Menon and one closed for Saanvi Reddy."
          loading="eager"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Filters across the top let you narrow to open cases when the list gets long.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Read the status</h2>
      <p>The status moves on its own as the counselling team works through the case.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pending</strong>: filed, and nobody has picked it up yet.</li>
        <li><strong>Acknowledged</strong>: a counsellor has taken it on.</li>
        <li><strong>In progress</strong>: they are actively working with the student.</li>
        <li><strong>Closed</strong>: the case is finished.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If something has been sitting at <strong>Pending</strong> longer than you expected and the
        situation has changed, raise it with your counselling team directly rather than filing a
        second referral.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">3</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Open one to see what you wrote</h2>
      <p>
        Click any row to expand it. You will see the description you submitted, the concerns you
        tagged, the class the student was in at the time, and the date you filed it.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-note">
        <p>
          <strong>The class is frozen at filing time.</strong> A referral you filed in September
          still reads "Grade 9-A" after the student moves class or moves up a year, so the record
          stays true to when you raised it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        If you have more to add after filing, use the note box on the expanded referral rather than
        starting a new one. It keeps everything on one thread for the counsellor.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>What you get back when it closes</h2>
      <p>
        A closed referral may carry a short summary from the counsellor. It is deliberately brief:
        enough for you to keep supporting the student in class, without handing over what was said in
        their sessions.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-note guide-privacy">
        <p>
          <strong>You will not see counselling notes.</strong> The counsellor keeps a separate
          clinical record that teachers have no access to. The closing summary is the one thing they
          choose to pass back to you, and they write it knowing you will read it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">5</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Withdraw one you filed by mistake</h2>
      <p>
        While a referral is still <strong>Pending</strong>, you can withdraw it from the expanded
        view. Once a counsellor has acknowledged it, the withdraw option goes away: at that point
        somebody has already read it and started acting on it, and quietly deleting the record would
        leave them working on something the system says never happened.
      </p>
      <p>If you need a case stopped after that point, speak to the counsellor directly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-footer">
    <h2>Things worth knowing</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Some cases appear without a teacher.</strong> If a student's own check-in flags
      distress, the counselling team gets a case automatically. Those never show up in your list or
      on your class roster, because they are the student's own result and not yours to see.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>A referral survives a class change.</strong> If the student transfers mid-term, the
      referral stays with you as the person who filed it, and the counsellor is told about the move.
    </p>
    <p>
      Stuck? Email <a href="mailto:admin@zengarden.co.in">admin@zengarden.co.in</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
